-- הסכם קיבוצי — הקצאת מסגרת עלות לתוספות שכר והטבות, קידום בדרגות וטבלאות
-- שכר (30.9.2016), "הסכם ספטמבר 2016": the wage agreement to 30.6.2018. Who
-- it covers; promotion under the base agreement's §38 rewritten from
-- 1.9.2016 (the conditions, the stay in months, the quotas and their rules
-- void) and again from 1.9.2017, with the teachers held back by the quotas
-- promoted from 1.9.2016 (a leaver from 1.8.2016); new combined-salary tables
-- from 1.9.2016 and an offsetting salary-protection supplement for the
-- existing teachers of grades 6.5–9 they pay less; a uniform shekel
-- supplement from 1.9.2016, stepped to 1.3.2019 and linked to the consumer
-- price index; the cost allocated from 1.3.2017, 1.3.2019 and 1.10.2019, as
-- the parties agree by 31.12.2016 or, failing that, by updates of the tables
-- (annexes ב, ג, ד) and a "2016 percentage supplement" for those off the
-- reform; the second one-time grant of 1,000; the 2016 agreement amended and
-- the agreement of 31.8.2016 replaced; budgetary pensioners (a bill the
-- Treasury announces); exhaustion of claims, industrial peace, the earlier
-- agreements, the follow-up committee and registration.
--
-- The annexes the agreement names — the tables א'1–א'7, ב1–ב30, ג1–ג30,
-- ד1–ד30 and annex ה' — are data at the end, each checked against the rule
-- that makes it (§§5(א), 7(ה) and 10). The agreement of 19.3.2017 amends §§3, 4, 5(ב),
-- 6(ב), 6(י), 7, 9(ב), 10 and 11; that is in its own file, which imports
-- this one.
--
-- Imported: the base agreement's §2 (language), §35 (an update of the
-- tables), §38 (promotion, which §4 rewrites) and §155 (the cost of a
-- framework agreement, which §11 exhausts); the 2016 agreement of 22.2.2016
-- (its salary base, which §7 measures the cost on, and the clauses §9 sets
-- aside); and the wages commissioner's circular 2016-1-13, whose record of a
-- teaching employee's employment in the grant's periods §8 asks again, in
-- the same periods. The agreements of 17.9.2013, 31.8.2016 (in its own file,
-- not yet on this branch's main line) and 7.5.2015, the supreme follow-up
-- committee's decision of 19.2.2015, the letters of 25.12.2008, 10.9.2007
-- and 11.11.2013, and the pension agreements are not imported: what a rule
-- needs of them is a named input.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `2016-02-22_ofek-hadash_hascam-2016_tables-and-sheklit`
IMPORT minimum_wage_law
IMPORT womens_work_law
IMPORT `tables-common`

-- A salary month: the salary paid FOR month m of year y (convention
-- dates.salary-month), which is paid in the month after.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `September 2016 salary month` y m IS
    y TIMES 12 PLUS m

-- What the parties must, may or may not do under this agreement.
DECLARE `September 2016 action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the promotion differences of §4(ג) and (ה)`
    `pay the shekel supplement and its differences`
    `agree on and anchor the allocation of the costs of §7(ב)–(ד)`
    `pay the payments of §7(ה)`
    `pay the second one-time grant`
    `support the legislation of §10(א)`
    `demand a further increase of the determining salary, a supplement or a benefit for these costs`
    `discuss the pensioners' arrangement without further cost`
    `negotiate further economic demands for the period to 30.6.2018`
    `declare a labour dispute or take organisational measures over the allocation of §7(ב)–(ד)`
    `strike, lock out or disrupt work over a matter the September 2016 agreement settles`
    `submit the agreement for registration as a special collective agreement`

-- The purposes a salary component may count for, as §§5(ב)(8)–(10), 6(ה)–
-- (ט), 7(ה)(2) and 8(ג)–(ה) list them.
DECLARE `September 2016 salary purpose` IS ONE OF
    `salary for every purpose`
    `the hour value for substitution hours and school activities`
    `the hour value`
    `the salary reduction for an hour of absence`
    `the payment under §31(ד) of the base agreement`
    `the payment under §33(ד) of the base agreement`
    `severance pay under the Severance Pay Law`
    `pensions`
    `pension-fund contributions for one insured in an accrual pension`
    `study-fund contributions and every other contribution or deduction usual on the combined salary`
    `provident-fund contributions of every kind`
    `the base of every pay supplement, by percentage or in shekels`
    `percentage supplements computed on the combined salary, but the 2001, 2008 and 2011 supplements`
    `yearly supplements and grants on the overtime hour-value base or the budgetary-pension determining salary`
    `the determining salary under §8 of the Pensions Law`
    `topping up to the minimum wage`
    `the salary base of the combined-salary tables`

-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: ‘משרה מלאה’ and
-- ‘היקף משרה’ here measure the position, as the base of a sum paid pro rata
-- to it or a threshold of eligibility; they set no working hour, day or
-- week, nor the pay of an hour the law counts.

§ `הסכם ספטמבר 2016 — 30.9.2016`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The document's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 The Registrar's stamp: registered on 15.01.2017 as no. 268/2016; no rule of the agreement.

-- The day of signing, written in by hand.
@ref akn:preamble/p3
`the September 2016 agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2016

-- The parties: the State, by the Treasury's acting wages commissioner and
-- the Ministry of Education's director-general, and the teachers' union, by
-- its secretary-general. (The State's short name is [לא קריא] in the corpus.)
@ref akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8
`the September 2016 agreement's parties` MEANS LIST `the State`, `the teachers' union`

-- akn:preamble/p6 "On the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p9 "On the other side"; no rule.

-- The recitals. The base agreement of 25.12.2008 ("הסכם רפורמת אופק חדש");
-- the full application of the 2011 framework's cost by the agreements of
-- 25.1.2011, 29.2.2012, 15.4.2013, 22.7.2013 and, from 1.1.2015, §155(א)(1)'s
-- default (imported: a uniform rise of the reform tables); the agreement of
-- 17.9.2013 ("הסכם 2013"); the general framework agreement of 18.4.2016 for
-- 2013–2017; the 2016 agreement of 22.2.2016 (imported); the conditions of
-- promotion of the base agreement and the supreme follow-up committee's
-- decision of 19.2.2015; the cost of the 2016 agreement allocated
-- otherwise; the amended framework of 8.8.2016; the special agreement of
-- 31.8.2016, which this one replaces. They state the history; the rules are
-- below.
@ref akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11
`the full framework's cost from 1.1.2015 is applied` MEANS
    `how a framework cost is applied` 90 FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `the full framework's cost from 1.1.2015 is applied` EQUALS `a uniform rise of the reform salary tables`

@ref akn:preamble/p12
`the 2013 agreement's period runs from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 27 8 2013

@ref akn:preamble/p13
`the general framework agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 18 4 2016

@ref akn:preamble/p14 akn:preamble/p16
`the 2016 agreement's cost period ends on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2015

#ASSERT `the 2016 agreement's cost period ends on` EQUALS `the 2016 agreement exhausts the claims for the period ending`

@ref akn:preamble/p15
`the 2015 follow-up committee decided on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 19 2 2015

@ref akn:preamble/p17
`the amended framework agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 8 8 2016

@ref akn:preamble/p18
`the 2016 agreement's cost is allocated otherwise than it says` MEANS TRUE

-- F-ofek-hadash-september-2016-d: the recital says the 2016 agreement was
-- to come into force on 1.9.2016; that agreement's own text names no such
-- day (its period is 27.8.2013–31.12.2015, and its §8(ב) promotes from
-- 1.9.2015).
@ref akn:preamble/p19
`the day the recital says the 2016 agreement was to come into force` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016

@ref akn:preamble/p20
`this agreement replaces the agreement of 31.8.2016` MEANS TRUE

-- akn:preamble/p21 A recital: the parties anchor what they agreed in a collective agreement; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p22 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

§§ `1 הוראות כלליות`

-- (א): the preamble is an inseparable part of the agreement.
@ref akn:art_1__para_a
GIVEN p IS A `part of the agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an inseparable part of the September 2016 agreement` p IF
    TRUE

-- (ב)–(ג): the masculine includes the feminine, the singular the plural (the
-- corpus reads the word [לא קריא]), and the reverse, unless said otherwise
-- expressly: the base agreement's §2.
@ref akn:art_1__para_b akn:art_1__para_c
GIVEN `written in` IS A `form of a word`, `read in` IS A `form of a word`, `expressly limited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a word of the September 2016 agreement reads in another form` `written in` `read in` `expressly limited` IF
    `a word written in one form reads in another` `written in` `read in` `expressly limited`

-- (ד): the headings are for convenience; nothing is learnt from them.
@ref akn:art_1__para_d
GIVEN `the reading without the headings` IS A STRING, `the reading the headings suggest` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the reading the September 2016 agreement takes` `the reading without the headings` `the reading the headings suggest` IS
    `the reading without the headings`

-- (ה): mentioning a letter does not change its normative standing.
@ref akn:art_1__para_e
GIVEN `the letter's standing` IS A NUMBER, `mentioned in this agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the standing of a letter the September 2016 agreement mentions` `the letter's standing` `mentioned in this agreement` IS
    `the letter's standing`

§§ `2 תחולה`

@desc An employee, as far as §2 of the September 2016 agreement asks.
DECLARE `employee under the September 2016 agreement` HAS
    `graded on the teaching employees' scale`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed in the State's service at the Ministry of Education` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the part in question is under the letters of 11.11.2013` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the part of the employment whose terms the wages commissioner's letters to the union of 11.11.2013 set

-- Every employee graded on the teaching employees' scale and employed in
-- the State's service at the Ministry of Education, save the part of the
-- employment the letters of 11.11.2013 set ("עובדי הוראה").
@ref akn:art_2/p1
GIVEN e IS AN `employee under the September 2016 agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a teaching employee of the September 2016 agreement` e IF
        e's `graded on the teaching employees' scale`
    AND e's `employed in the State's service at the Ministry of Education`
    AND NOT e's `the part in question is under the letters of 11.11.2013`

§§ `3 תקופת ההסכם`

-- To 30.6.2018. (The agreement of 19.3.2017, §2(א), makes it 30.6.2019.)
@ref akn:art_3/p1
`the September 2016 agreement runs until` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2018

§§ `4 קידום בדרגות`

-- ¶1: for the avoidance of doubt, the section applies to the teaching
-- employees to whom §38 of the base agreement, as amended, applies.
@ref akn:art_4/p1
GIVEN `§38 applies to the teacher` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§4 of the September 2016 agreement applies` `§38 applies to the teacher` IF
    `§38 applies to the teacher`

`the September 2016 promotion rules start` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016
`the unified promotion conditions start` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2017

-- (א)(2): §38(ב) of the base agreement (as amended, the 2015 decision
-- included) becomes, from 1.9.2016, months of stay in the grade below: 30
-- to grades 2 and 3, 36 to grades 4–6, 48 to grades 7–9.
@ref akn:art_4__para_a akn:art_4__para_a__subpara_2
GIVEN `to grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months in the grade below for promotion from 1.9.2016 to` `to grade` IS
    BRANCH IF `to grade` AT MOST 3 THEN 30
           IF `to grade` AT MOST 6 THEN 36
           OTHERWISE 48

#ASSERT map `months in the grade below for promotion from 1.9.2016 to` (LIST 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9) EQUALS LIST 30, 30, 36, 36, 36, 48, 48, 48
-- From grade 1 to grade 9: 312 months, where the base agreement asked 22 years.
#ASSERT sum (map `months in the grade below for promotion from 1.9.2016 to` (LIST 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9)) EQUALS 312
#ASSERT 12 TIMES sum (map `years in the grade below for promotion to` (LIST 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9)) EQUALS 264

@desc A teacher in a grade, as far as §38 as §4 of the September 2016 agreement rewrites it asks.
DECLARE `teacher for promotion from 1.9.2016` HAS
    `the candidate`                       IS A `candidate` @desc the base agreement's §38 record: the grade, the periods in it (counted by §38(ג)–(ד), which stand), the Ministry's criteria
    `a formative evaluation was made in the grade below` IS A BOOLEAN @desc by the Ministry's professional directions, with the national authority for measurement and evaluation, after consulting the union

-- The months in the grade, as §38(ג)–(ד) count its years.
GIVEN t IS A `teacher for promotion from 1.9.2016`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months counted in the grade for §4` t IS
    12 TIMES `years counted in the grade` (t's `the candidate`'s `periods in the grade`)

-- (א)(1): from 1.9.2016 §38(א) reads: (א) to grades 2–6, (1) the stay of
-- (ב) and (2) the Ministry's criteria by its letter of 25.12.2008; (א1) to
-- grades 7–9, also a formative evaluation in the grade below. (ו): from
-- 1.9.2017 (תשע"ח) (א) and (א1) become one (א): to grades 2–9, all three.
-- (א)(3): §38(ה)–(יא) are void — the evaluation that recommends promotion,
-- the quotas of grades 7–9, the yearly check and the order, the longest
-- hold-back: a teacher who meets the conditions is promoted.
@ref akn:art_4__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_4__para_a__subpara_3 akn:art_4__para_f
GIVEN t IS A `teacher for promotion from 1.9.2016`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the conditions for the next grade under §4 of the September 2016 agreement` t d IF
        t's `the candidate`'s grade AT LEAST 1
    AND t's `the candidate`'s grade AT MOST 8
    AND `months counted in the grade for §4` t AT LEAST `months in the grade below for promotion from 1.9.2016 to` (t's `the candidate`'s grade PLUS 1)
    AND t's `the candidate`'s `meets the Ministry's criteria`
    AND (   t's `a formative evaluation was made in the grade below`
         OR (    t's `the candidate`'s grade PLUS 1 AT MOST 6
             AND NOT d `is on or after` `the unified promotion conditions start`))

-- (א)(3): the quotas of §38(ז), and the rules of (ח)–(יא) on them, bind
-- only before 1.9.2016.
@ref akn:art_4__para_a__subpara_3
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the quotas of §38(ז) bind on` d IF
    NOT d `is on or after` `the September 2016 promotion rules start`

-- (ב): (א) reaches also the teachers who would have been entitled to a
-- promotion from 1.9.2016 on but for the agreement of 31.8.2016 (which put
-- off the periods; in its own file).
@ref akn:art_4__para_b
GIVEN `would have been promoted from 1.9.2016 but for the agreement of 31.8.2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement of 31.8.2016 holds back the promotion` `would have been promoted from 1.9.2016 but for the agreement of 31.8.2016` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `a candidate in grade` IS A NUMBER, `months in it` IS A NUMBER, `criteria` IS A BOOLEAN, `formative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `teacher for promotion from 1.9.2016`
DECIDE `a teacher from 1.9.2016 in grade` `a candidate in grade` `months in it` `criteria` `formative` IS
    `teacher for promotion from 1.9.2016` WITH
        `the candidate` IS `candidate` WITH
            grade                         IS `a candidate in grade`
            `periods in the grade`        IS LIST (`a period of` `work in the grade` (`months in it` DIVIDED BY 12) FALSE FALSE)
            `meets the Ministry's criteria` IS `criteria`
            `evaluation recommends promotion` IS FALSE
            `evaluation score`            IS 0
        `a formative evaluation was made in the grade below` IS `formative`

-- To grade 6 in 2016–17 without a formative evaluation; not from 1.9.2017.
#ASSERT `meets the conditions for the next grade under §4 of the September 2016 agreement` (`a teacher from 1.9.2016 in grade` 5 36 TRUE FALSE) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `meets the conditions for the next grade under §4 of the September 2016 agreement` (`a teacher from 1.9.2016 in grade` 5 36 TRUE FALSE) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2017)
-- To grade 7: 48 months and a formative evaluation; 47 months are not enough.
#ASSERT `meets the conditions for the next grade under §4 of the September 2016 agreement` (`a teacher from 1.9.2016 in grade` 6 48 TRUE TRUE) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `meets the conditions for the next grade under §4 of the September 2016 agreement` (`a teacher from 1.9.2016 in grade` 6 47 TRUE TRUE) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `meets the conditions for the next grade under §4 of the September 2016 agreement` (`a teacher from 1.9.2016 in grade` 6 48 TRUE FALSE) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016)
#ASSERT `the quotas of §38(ז) bind on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `the quotas of §38(ז) bind on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016)

@desc A teaching employee held back from grade 7, 8 or 9 before 1.9.2016, as far as §4(ג) and (ה) ask.
DECLARE `teacher held back before 1.9.2016` HAS
    `held back by a rule §4(א)(3) voids` IS A BOOLEAN @desc met the conditions for grade 7, 8 or 9 before 1.9.2016 and was held back by §38(ה)–(יא)
    `development hours for the grade acquired by 31.8.2016` IS A BOOLEAN @desc by the Ministry's letter to the union of 25.12.2008, not in the corpus
    `the stay of §38(ו) as the 2015 decision worded it was met by 31.8.2016` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the follow-up committee's decision of 19.2.2015 sets the periods; an input here
    `months of stay in the grade below on 1.9.2016` IS A NUMBER
    `evaluation results suffice by the indices of תשע"ב` IS A BOOLEAN
    `evaluated by the Ministry's directions on the eve of the signing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `left the State's service on 31.8.2016` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (ג): one held back by a voided rule is promoted to grade 7, 8 or 9 back
-- from 1.9.2016 if (1) he acquired the development hours by 31.8.2016, (2)
-- he met the stay of §38(ו), as the 2015 decision worded it, by 31.8.2016,
-- and (3) with a stay under 48 months on 1.9.2016, his evaluation results
-- suffice by the indices of תשע"ב; with 48 months or more, he was evaluated
-- by the Ministry's directions on the eve of the signing. (ה): one who left
-- the service on 31.8.2016 and would have met (ג) but for leaving is
-- promoted back from 1.8.2016. (ד): mentioning the letter of 25.12.2008
-- changes nothing in how the Ministry applies it.
@ref akn:art_4__para_c akn:art_4__para_c/p2 akn:art_4__para_c__subpara_1 akn:art_4__para_c__subpara_2 akn:art_4__para_c__subpara_3 akn:art_4__para_c__subpara_3/p2 akn:art_4__para_c__subpara_3/p3 akn:art_4__para_c__subpara_3/p4 akn:art_4__para_d akn:art_4__para_e
GIVEN t IS A `teacher held back before 1.9.2016`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets §4(ג) of the September 2016 agreement` t IF
        t's `held back by a rule §4(א)(3) voids`
    AND t's `development hours for the grade acquired by 31.8.2016`
    AND t's `the stay of §38(ו) as the 2015 decision worded it was met by 31.8.2016`
    AND (IF t's `months of stay in the grade below on 1.9.2016` LESS THAN 48
         THEN t's `evaluation results suffice by the indices of תשע"ב`
         ELSE t's `evaluated by the Ministry's directions on the eve of the signing`)

GIVEN t IS A `teacher held back before 1.9.2016`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `promoted back under §4(ג) from` t IS
    IF `meets §4(ג) of the September 2016 agreement` t
    THEN (IF t's `left the State's service on 31.8.2016`
          THEN JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2016)
          ELSE JUST `the September 2016 promotion rules start`)
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN months IS A NUMBER, results IS A BOOLEAN, evaluated IS A BOOLEAN, left IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `teacher held back before 1.9.2016`
DECIDE `a held-back teacher with` months results evaluated left IS
    `teacher held back before 1.9.2016` WITH
        `held back by a rule §4(א)(3) voids` IS TRUE
        `development hours for the grade acquired by 31.8.2016` IS TRUE
        `the stay of §38(ו) as the 2015 decision worded it was met by 31.8.2016` IS TRUE
        `months of stay in the grade below on 1.9.2016` IS months
        `evaluation results suffice by the indices of תשע"ב` IS results
        `evaluated by the Ministry's directions on the eve of the signing` IS evaluated
        `left the State's service on 31.8.2016` IS left

#ASSERT `promoted back under §4(ג) from` (`a held-back teacher with` 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016)
#ASSERT `promoted back under §4(ג) from` (`a held-back teacher with` 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `promoted back under §4(ג) from` (`a held-back teacher with` 48 FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016)
#ASSERT `promoted back under §4(ג) from` (`a held-back teacher with` 48 FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2016)

-- (ז): the section takes nothing from the base agreement's other rules of
-- promotion, or the parties' other agreements on it, unless it says so.
@ref akn:art_4__para_g
`§4 of the September 2016 agreement takes away from other rules of promotion it does not name` MEANS FALSE

-- (ח): the differences of (ג) and (ה) are paid from the salary for October
-- 2016 (paid in November) and no later than the salary for November 2016
-- (paid in December).
@ref akn:art_4__para_h
`paying the promotion differences` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `pay the promotion differences of §4(ג) and (ה)`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the State` BECAUSE "§4(ח): the differences are paid with the salary for November 2016 at the latest"

GIVEN `paid with the salary for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the promotion differences are paid in time` `paid with the salary for` IF
    `paid with the salary for` AT MOST `September 2016 salary month` 2016 11

#ASSERT `the promotion differences are paid in time` (`September 2016 salary month` 2016 11)
#ASSERT NOT `the promotion differences are paid in time` (`September 2016 salary month` 2016 12)

-- F-ofek-hadash-september-2016-d: §9(ג) sets §8 of the 2016 agreement aside
-- "from 1.9.2016" (§9 ¶2), while that §8(ב) placed the teachers it promoted
-- in grades 7–9 back from 1.9.2015. The reading adopted (convention
-- dates.commencement: §9 ¶2's day dates every clause under it): the 2016
-- agreement's §8 governs from 1.9.2015 to 31.8.2016, and gives no grade
-- from 1.9.2016, when §4 above governs promotion (its (ג) for those the
-- quotas held back).
GIVEN t IS A `teacher for the 2016 one-time promotion`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the grade the 2016 agreement's §8 gives under §9 of the September 2016 agreement` t d IS
    IF d `is on or after` `the September 2016 promotion rules start`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the grade under §8 of the 2016 agreement on` t d)

#ASSERT `the grade the 2016 agreement's §8 gives under §9 of the September 2016 agreement` `a grade-6 teacher of three years` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) EQUALS NOTHING

`the 2016 agreement's §8 promotes from a day before §9 sets it aside` MEANS
        `the grade the 2016 agreement's §8 gives under §9 of the September 2016 agreement` `a grade-6 teacher of three years` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2015) EQUALS JUST 7
    AND `the 2016 one-time promotion takes effect from` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2016)
    AND NOT (`the day the recital says the 2016 agreement was to come into force` EQUALS `the 2016 one-time promotion takes effect from`)
#ASSERT `the 2016 agreement's §8 promotes from a day before §9 sets it aside`

§§ `5 עדכון טבלאות השכר המשולב ותוספת שמירת שכר מתקזזת`

-- ¶1: the section applies to the teaching employees of §4.
-- (א): from 1.9.2016 ("המועד הקובע") the combined-salary tables are
-- annexes א'1–א'7, updated at the dates and by the rates of the
-- cost-of-living supplement (§35's updates, imported). The annexes are
-- data at the end (`annexes א' of 30.9.2016`). The 2016 agreement of
-- 22.2.2016 attaches tables under the same numbers, updated to the same
-- day; they are not these: annexes א'1–א'6 here step grades 7–9 by 7.5%
-- where those step them by 7.8% and 8.5%, and only א'7 is the same table
-- (checked at the end).
@ref akn:art_5/p1 akn:art_5__para_a akn:art_5__para_a/p2
`the September 2016 determining date` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016

GIVEN annex IS A NUMBER
      seniority IS A NUMBER
      `the grade` IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
      `cost-of-living updates` IS A LIST OF `table update`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the September 2016 table salary on` annex seniority `the grade` d `cost-of-living updates` IS
    IF d `is on or after` `the September 2016 determining date`
    THEN CONSIDER `the cell of the September 2016 annexes א'1–א'7` annex seniority `the grade`
         WHEN JUST c THEN JUST (`the cell on` c d `cost-of-living updates`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `the September 2016 determining date` EQUALS `the 2016 determining date`

@desc A teaching employee on the determining date, as far as §5(ב) asks.
DECLARE `teacher at the September 2016 tables` HAS
    `grade before the determining date`    IS A NUMBER
    `paid by the tables in force to 31.8.2016` IS A BOOLEAN
    `promoted on 1.9.2016`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `away on 1.9.2016`                     IS A `away on the determining date`
    `old table salary`                     IS A NUMBER @desc the table salary he would have been paid on 1.9.2016 by the tables in force on 31.8.2016 (for one away, had he been at work)
    `old allowances`                       IS A NUMBER @desc role allowances, the doctorate allowance and the trailing management allowance, as far as entitled, on the old tables (for one away, those determined for his return)
    `new table salary`                     IS A NUMBER @desc his table salary on 1.9.2016 by annexes א'1–א'7 (for one away, had he been at work)
    `new allowances`                       IS A NUMBER
    `seniority rise of the old table salary on 1.9.2016` IS A NUMBER @desc with its effect on the allowances
    `seniority rise of the new table salary on 1.9.2016` IS A NUMBER @desc with its effect on the allowances

DECLARE `away on the determining date` IS ONE OF
    `at work`
    `in maternity and parenthood under the Women's Employment Law`
    `on unpaid leave, a sabbatical or another absence without salary`

-- (ב)(1): an existing teacher is one of §4's teachers who (א) was in grade
-- 6.5, 7, 7.5, 8, 8.5 or 9 before the determining date, paid by the tables
-- in force to 31.8.2016; (ב) whose new table salary on it is lower than
-- the table salary he would have been paid but for the new tables; and (ג)
-- who was not promoted on 1.9.2016.
@ref akn:art_5__para_b akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_1/p2 akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_1__cls_a akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_1__cls_b akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_1__cls_c
GIVEN t IS A `teacher at the September 2016 tables`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing teacher under §5(ב)` t IF
        elem (t's `grade before the determining date`) (LIST 6.5, 7, 7.5, 8, 8.5, 9)
    AND t's `paid by the tables in force to 31.8.2016`
    AND t's `new table salary` LESS THAN t's `old table salary`
    AND NOT t's `promoted on 1.9.2016`

-- (ב)(2): from the first salary paid by the new tables, an existing
-- teacher is entitled, on top of the table salary, to a monthly shekel
-- supplement Z = X − Y: X the old table salary with the allowances, less
-- the rise of the table salary for his seniority on the determining date
-- and its effect on the allowances, by the tables in force on 31.8.2016; Y
-- the new, less the same rise on the new tables. (3)–(4): for one in
-- maternity and parenthood, or on unpaid leave, a sabbatical or another
-- absence without salary, on the determining date, X and Y are what would
-- have been paid but for it, with the allowances set for the return (the
-- record's fields say so).
@ref akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_2/p3 akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_2/p4 akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_2/p5 akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_3 akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_4
GIVEN t IS A `teacher at the September 2016 tables`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `X under §5(ב)(2)` t IS
    t's `old table salary` PLUS t's `old allowances` MINUS t's `seniority rise of the old table salary on 1.9.2016`

GIVEN t IS A `teacher at the September 2016 tables`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Y under §5(ב)(2)` t IS
    t's `new table salary` PLUS t's `new allowances` MINUS t's `seniority rise of the new table salary on 1.9.2016`

GIVEN t IS A `teacher at the September 2016 tables`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Z under §5(ב)(2)` t IS
    IF `an existing teacher under §5(ב)` t
    THEN `X under §5(ב)(2)` t MINUS `Y under §5(ב)(2)` t
    ELSE 0

-- (ב)(5): notwithstanding (2)–(4), Z shrinks at every rise in the salary,
-- from any cause save a change in the role allowances, by the rise, from
-- its day, the determining date included; its amount is then C. The text
-- writes "P − Z (as (2) computed it) = C", P being the rise.
-- F-ofek-hadash-september-2016-a: the formula as printed gives P − Z, which
-- is below zero whenever the rise is smaller than the supplement; the words
-- say Z shrinks by the rise. The reading adopted (convention
-- reading.misprint): C = Z − P, never below zero (amounts.never-negative).
@ref akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_5 akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_5/p2 akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_5/p3
GIVEN z IS A NUMBER, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `C under §5(ב)(5)` z p IS
    `not below zero` (z MINUS p)

GIVEN z IS A NUMBER, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `C as §5(ב)(5)'s formula prints it` z p IS
    p MINUS z

`§5(ב)(5)'s formula gives a negative supplement where the words shrink it` MEANS
        `C as §5(ב)(5)'s formula prints it` 220 100 LESS THAN 0
    AND `C under §5(ב)(5)` 220 100 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `§5(ב)(5)'s formula gives a negative supplement where the words shrink it`

-- (ב)(6): one in grade 9 on 31.8.2016 has (5) applied only to the rise on
-- 1.9.2016; one in grade 6.5–8.5, every month.
@ref akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_6
GIVEN `grade on 31.8.2016` IS A NUMBER, `day of the rise` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a rise shrinks the supplement under §5(ב)(6)` `grade on 31.8.2016` `day of the rise` IF
    (NOT `grade on 31.8.2016` EQUALS 9) OR `day of the rise` EQUALS `the September 2016 determining date`

#ASSERT `a rise shrinks the supplement under §5(ב)(6)` 9 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `a rise shrinks the supplement under §5(ב)(6)` 9 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2017)
#ASSERT `a rise shrinks the supplement under §5(ב)(6)` 8 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2017)

-- (ב)(7): one entitled to another salary-protection supplement too: a rise
-- shrinks this supplement first, and only what is left of it the other, by
-- the agreements on it — the 2016 agreement's §7(ד) rule, imported.
@ref akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_7
GIVEN c IS A NUMBER, rise IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the rise left for another supplement under §5(ב)(7)` c rise IS
    `the rise left for another salary-protection supplement` c rise

-- not weighed against `the Severance Pay Law`: §§5(ב)(8), 6(ו) and
-- 7(ה)(2)(ד) counts the pay-keeping supplement (C), the shekel supplement
-- and the 2016 percentage supplement in the wage severance is computed on,
-- and §8(ג) leaves the grant out of it. Which components count, §13 sends
-- to the regulations, which compute that wage by the collective agreement
-- that applies (as the takanon's §1.28.2.3 brings them): a component
-- counted adds to the severance, and for one left out the agreement's word
-- is what the law looks to; §13ב's minimum-wage floor holds whatever is
-- counted.

-- (ב)(8): C is salary for every purpose, and counts for the hour value of
-- substitution and school activities, the reduction for an hour of
-- absence, the payment "under §31(ד) of the base agreement", severance
-- pay, pensions, accrual-pension contributions, the study fund and every
-- other contribution or deduction usual on the combined salary. (9): it is
-- in the base of no pay supplement; (10): save yearly supplements and grants
-- on the overtime hour-value base or the budgetary-pension determining
-- salary.
-- F-ofek-hadash-september-2016-b: the base agreement's §31 has (א) and (ב)
-- only (its module encodes those two); the same words in §6(ו) and §8(ג)
-- name §33(ד), the payment beyond a full position. The reading adopted
-- (convention instruments.missing-clause, the lawyer's pick MMS-311): the
-- reference stays without a target, and the rest of the sentence applies
-- as written — C is salary for every purpose, so the payment of §33(ד)
-- counts it all the same.
@ref akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_8 akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_9 akn:art_5__para_b__subpara_10
GIVEN p IS A `September 2016 salary purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the protection supplement C counts for` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `the base of every pay supplement, by percentage or in shekels` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `percentage supplements computed on the combined salary, but the 2001, 2008 and 2011 supplements` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `topping up to the minimum wage` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the salary base of the combined-salary tables` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `provident-fund contributions of every kind` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

`the paragraphs of the base agreement's §31` MEANS LIST "(א)", "(ב)"

`§5(ב)(8) names a §31(ד) the base agreement does not have` MEANS
        NOT elem "(ד)" `the paragraphs of the base agreement's §31`
    AND `the protection supplement C counts for` `the payment under §33(ד) of the base agreement`
#ASSERT `§5(ב)(8) names a §31(ד) the base agreement does not have`

`an existing grade-8 teacher` MEANS
    `teacher at the September 2016 tables` WITH
        `grade before the determining date`    IS 8
        `paid by the tables in force to 31.8.2016` IS TRUE
        `promoted on 1.9.2016`                 IS FALSE
        `away on 1.9.2016`                     IS `at work`
        `old table salary`                     IS 14000
        `old allowances`                       IS 1400
        `new table salary`                     IS 13700
        `new allowances`                       IS 1370
        `seniority rise of the old table salary on 1.9.2016` IS 154
        `seniority rise of the new table salary on 1.9.2016` IS 151

#ASSERT `Z under §5(ב)(2)` `an existing grade-8 teacher` EQUALS 327
#ASSERT `C under §5(ב)(5)` 327 400 EQUALS 0

§§ `6 תוספת שקלית אחידה לעובדי הוראה`

-- (א)–(ב): from 1.9.2016 the teaching employees are entitled to a monthly
-- shekel supplement ("התוספת השקלית לעובד הוראה"); for a full position:
-- 108.18 to 28.2.2017; 193.64 to 31.5.2018; 282.35 to 30.11.2018; 415.41
-- to 28.2.2019; 543.33 from 1.3.2019. (The agreement of 19.3.2017, §2(ה),
-- replaces (ב).)
@desc A period of a shekel supplement for a full position.
DECLARE `shekel supplement period` HAS
    `period from`   IS A DATE
    `period amount` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_6__para_a akn:art_6__para_b akn:art_6__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_6__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_6__para_b__subpara_3 akn:art_6__para_b__subpara_4 akn:art_6__para_b__subpara_5
`the September 2016 shekel supplement periods` MEANS
    LIST `shekel supplement period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) 108.18,
         `shekel supplement period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) 193.64,
         `shekel supplement period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2018) 282.35,
         `shekel supplement period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) 415.41,
         `shekel supplement period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019) 543.33

-- The amount of the last period begun by a day; none before the first.
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `shekel supplement period`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full-position amount in force` ps d IS
    foldl (GIVEN acc, p YIELD IF d `is on or after` (p's `period from`) THEN p's `period amount` ELSE acc) 0 ps

#ASSERT `the full-position amount in force` `the September 2016 shekel supplement periods` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2017) EQUALS 108.18
#ASSERT `the full-position amount in force` `the September 2016 shekel supplement periods` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) EQUALS 193.64
#ASSERT `the full-position amount in force` `the September 2016 shekel supplement periods` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019) EQUALS 543.33
#ASSERT `the full-position amount in force` `the September 2016 shekel supplement periods` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2016) EQUALS 0

-- (ד): from January 2017, once a year in January, the amount is updated by
-- the rise of the new index (December of the year before) over the
-- previous one (December of the year before the previous update; for the
-- first, December 2015). A fall makes no update; the update waits for one
-- that rises above the last index used, the fall offset in full. So the
-- index in force is the highest December index from 2015 to the December
-- before the last January update, and the linkage factor is it over
-- December 2015's.
-- F-ofek-hadash-september-2016-e: (ד) prices the supplement from December
-- 2015, and (ב) prints amounts that begin after updates were made. The
-- reading adopted (convention reading.consistent; the exception is
-- recorded under dates.update-in-force): every amount (ב) sets carries
-- every update from December 2015.
@desc A December consumer price index.
DECLARE `December index` HAS
    `index year`  IS A NUMBER
    `index value` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_6__para_d akn:art_6__para_d/p2 akn:art_6__para_d/p3 akn:art_6__para_d/p4 akn:art_6__para_d/p5 akn:art_6__para_d/p6
GIVEN decembers IS A LIST OF `December index`
      `the year of the last January update` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the shekel supplement's linkage factor` decembers `the year of the last January update` IS
    foldl max `the December 2015 index` (map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `index value`) (filter (GIVEN i YIELD i's `index year` AT LEAST 2015 AND i's `index year` LESS THAN `the year of the last January update`) decembers))
        DIVIDED BY `the December 2015 index`
    WHERE
        `the December 2015 index` MEANS foldl (GIVEN acc, i YIELD IF i's `index year` EQUALS 2015 THEN i's `index value` ELSE acc) 1 decembers

-- The year of the last January update on a day: none before January 2017.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the year of the last January update on` d IS
    IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2017)
    THEN DATE_YEAR d
    ELSE 2016

-- (ג): in proportion to the position, compared with a full position; the
-- text sets no ceiling (convention position.above-full).
@ref akn:art_6__para_c
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `shekel supplement period`
      decembers IS A LIST OF `December index`
      `position share` IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the shekel supplement for a teaching employee` ps decembers `position share` d IS
    `the linked full-position amount` `pro rata to a position of` `position share`
    WHERE
        `the linked full-position amount` MEANS
            `the full-position amount in force` ps d TIMES `the shekel supplement's linkage factor` decembers (`the year of the last January update on` d)

-- Hypothetical indices, to show the rule: 2016 falls, 2017 rises above
-- 2015, 2018 falls below 2017.
`hypothetical December indices` MEANS
    LIST `December index` 2015 100, `December index` 2016 99.8, `December index` 2017 100.2, `December index` 2018 100.1

#ASSERT `the shekel supplement's linkage factor` `hypothetical December indices` 2017 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the shekel supplement's linkage factor` `hypothetical December indices` 2018 EQUALS 1.002
#ASSERT `the shekel supplement's linkage factor` `hypothetical December indices` 2019 EQUALS 1.002
#ASSERT `the shekel supplement for a teaching employee` `the September 2016 shekel supplement periods` `hypothetical December indices` 0.5 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2016) EQUALS 54.09

`§6(ב) prints amounts that begin after §6(ד)'s first update` MEANS
    any (GIVEN p YIELD p's `period from` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2017)) `the September 2016 shekel supplement periods`
#ASSERT `§6(ב) prints amounts that begin after §6(ד)'s first update`

-- (ה): not counted in topping up to the minimum wage; an "excluded
-- supplement" under the 2015 temporary minimum-wage law. (ו): salary for
-- every purpose, counted for the hour value of substitution and school
-- activities, the reduction for an hour of absence, the payment of §33(ד)
-- of the base agreement, severance pay, accrual-pension and study-fund
-- contributions and every contribution or deduction usual on the combined
-- salary. (ז): in the base of no supplement; (ח): save yearly supplements
-- and grants on the overtime hour-value base or the budgetary-pension
-- determining salary. (ט): the government states that under §8 of the
-- Pensions Law it counts in the determining salary.
@ref akn:art_6__para_e akn:art_6__para_f akn:art_6__para_g akn:art_6__para_h akn:art_6__para_i
GIVEN p IS A `September 2016 salary purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shekel supplement counts for` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `topping up to the minimum wage` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the base of every pay supplement, by percentage or in shekels` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `percentage supplements computed on the combined salary, but the 2001, 2008 and 2011 supplements` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the salary base of the combined-salary tables` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `provident-fund contributions of every kind` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the payment under §31(ד) of the base agreement` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

#ASSERT `the shekel supplement counts for` `the determining salary under §8 of the Pensions Law`
#ASSERT `the shekel supplement counts for` `yearly supplements and grants on the overtime hour-value base or the budgetary-pension determining salary`

@ref akn:art_6__para_e
`the shekel supplement is an excluded supplement under the 2015 minimum-wage law` MEANS TRUE

-- What (ה) leaves for the minimum-wage top-up: the Minimum Wage Law's
-- top-up (l4/laws/minimum-wage-law.l4, §2), on the pay that counts for it
-- with the supplement not among it. The minimum owed is the law's, whose
-- amount is published under its §6, so it is an argument here.
GIVEN `the minimum wage` IS A NUMBER @desc the minimum owed for the month under §2 of the Minimum Wage Law
      `the pay that counts` IS A NUMBER @desc the pay §3 of the Minimum Wage Law counts, the shekel supplement apart
      `the shekel supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the minimum-wage top-up beside the shekel supplement` `the minimum wage` `the pay that counts` `the shekel supplement` IS
    `the top-up the Minimum Wage Law requires` `the minimum wage` (`the pay that counts` PLUS `the part of the supplement counted`)
    WHERE
        `the part of the supplement counted` MEANS
            IF `the shekel supplement counts for` `topping up to the minimum wage` THEN `the shekel supplement` ELSE 0

-- The ministry's salary simulator (educalc), salary months January 2018 and
-- January 2019, grade 1 of the בכירים scale, first year: combined salary
-- 4,354.23 and the 2016 shekel supplement 194.03 (2018); its two
-- minimum-wage lines, 178.70 and 573.04, bring the three to 5,300.00, the
-- minimum wage then. They count the supplement: by (ה) the top-up is
-- 945.77, the supplement more (card min-wage-shekel-2016).
`the simulator's 2018 top-up counts the shekel supplement (ה) leaves out` MEANS
        `the minimum-wage top-up beside the shekel supplement` 5300 4354.23 194.03 EQUALS 945.77
    AND 178.70 PLUS 573.04 EQUALS 5300 MINUS 4354.23 MINUS 194.03
#ASSERT `the simulator's 2018 top-up counts the shekel supplement (ה) leaves out`

-- Against the Minimum Wage Law's floor (MMS-601). As the law reads now, its
-- §3(ב)(3) counts "a fixed supplement paid for the work", which a monthly
-- shekel supplement is (convention
-- instruments.minimum-wage-fixed-supplement); so the law's own top-up
-- counts the supplement, and (ה), leaving it out, makes the top-up larger:
-- it adds to the law (§11) and is never below its floor. The simulator's
-- 2018 lines are the law's top-up as it reads now — the floor, and not the
-- more (ה) gives. (Which supplements counted in 2016–2019 turned on the
-- temporary provision of תשע"ה-2015, whose "excluded supplement" (ה)
-- names; it has lapsed and is outside the pin.)
GIVEN `the minimum wage` IS A NUMBER, `the pay that counts` IS A NUMBER, `the shekel supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `(ה)'s top-up falls below the Minimum Wage Law` `the minimum wage` `the pay that counts` `the shekel supplement` IF
    `the instrument's top-up falls below the Minimum Wage Law`
        (`the minimum-wage top-up beside the shekel supplement` `the minimum wage` `the pay that counts` `the shekel supplement`)
        `the minimum wage`
        (`the pay that counts` PLUS `the shekel supplement`)

#ASSERT NOT `(ה)'s top-up falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4354.23 194.03
#ASSERT NOT `(ה)'s top-up falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 5200 194.03
#ASSERT 178.70 PLUS 573.04 EQUALS `the top-up the Minimum Wage Law requires` 5300 (4354.23 PLUS 194.03)

-- (י): "the payments arising from §6(ו)" are paid from the salary for
-- October 2016 and no later than the salary for November 2016, with the
-- differences from 1.9.2016.
-- F-ofek-hadash-september-2016-c: §6(ו) is the list of what the supplement
-- counts for; the payments of the supplement arise from (א)–(ב), and (י)
-- names no time for them. The reading adopted (convention reading.misprint):
-- (י) times the supplement itself and the payments (ו) derives from it.
@ref akn:art_6__para_j
`paying the shekel supplement from October 2016` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `pay the shekel supplement and its differences`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the State` BECAUSE "§6(י): from the salary for October 2016, the November salary at the latest"

GIVEN `first paid with the salary for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the first day of the differences paid with the supplement` `first paid with the salary for` IS
    IF `first paid with the salary for` AT MOST `September 2016 salary month` 2016 11
    THEN `September 2016 salary month` 2016 9
    ELSE `first paid with the salary for`

`the clause (י) times` MEANS "6(ו)"
`the clauses that pay the supplement` MEANS LIST "6(א)", "6(ב)"
`§6(י) times the payments of a clause that pays nothing` MEANS
    NOT elem `the clause (י) times` `the clauses that pay the supplement`
#ASSERT `§6(י) times the payments of a clause that pays nothing`

§§ `7 הקצאת עלות החל מיום 1.3.2017, 1.3.2019 ו־1.10.2019`

-- (א): "the salary base" of (ב)–(ד) is §6 of the 2016 agreement (imported).
@ref akn:art_7__para_a
GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `component of the 2016 salary base`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary base of §7` cs IS
    `the 2016 salary base` cs

-- (ב)–(ד): a cost of 0.26% of the base from 1.3.2017, 0.25% from 1.3.2019 and
-- 0.75% from 1.10.2019, for pay supplements and benefits, as the parties
-- agree and anchor in a collective agreement by 31.12.2016.
@desc One allocation of §7's cost.
DECLARE `September 2016 allocation` HAS
    `allocation from` IS A DATE
    `allocation rate` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_7__para_b akn:art_7__para_c akn:art_7__para_d
`the September 2016 allocations` MEANS
    LIST `September 2016 allocation` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) (0.26%),
         `September 2016 allocation` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019) (0.25%),
         `September 2016 allocation` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2019) (0.75%)

`the day §7's allocations are to be agreed by` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2016

@ref akn:art_7__para_b akn:art_7__para_c akn:art_7__para_d
`agreeing on §7's allocations` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MAY   `agree on and anchor the allocation of the costs of §7(ב)–(ד)`
    WITHIN DATE_SERIAL `the day §7's allocations are to be agreed by` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the September 2016 agreement was signed on`

-- (ה): failing an agreement by 31.12.2016, the default.
DECLARE `way §7's cost is allocated` IS ONE OF
    `as the parties agreed in a collective agreement`
    `the reform tables updated`
    `the 2016 percentage supplement and the shekel supplements updated`
    `not by §7(ה)`

@desc A teaching employee, as far as §7(ה) asks.
DECLARE `teacher under §7(ה)` HAS
    `on the reform's terms`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the part in question is in a college that trains teaching employees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the part in question is a supervision or headquarters role under the agreement of 5.7.2010` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (ה)(1): the tables of the reform's teachers, and of the supervision and
-- headquarters staff of 5.7.2010 (for that part), are updated; not the part
-- in a college. (ה)(2): those off the reform, and the colleges' teachers,
-- get the 2016 percentage supplement; not the part in supervision or
-- headquarters.
@ref akn:art_7__para_e akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_1 akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_2
GIVEN t IS A `teacher under §7(ה)`, `agreed by 31.12.2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `way §7's cost is allocated`
DECIDE `how §7's cost reaches` t `agreed by 31.12.2016` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `agreed by 31.12.2016` THEN `as the parties agreed in a collective agreement`
        IF t's `the part in question is a supervision or headquarters role under the agreement of 5.7.2010` THEN `the reform tables updated`
        IF t's `the part in question is in a college that trains teaching employees` THEN `the 2016 percentage supplement and the shekel supplements updated`
        IF t's `on the reform's terms` THEN `the reform tables updated`
        OTHERWISE `the 2016 percentage supplement and the shekel supplements updated`

-- (ה)(1), (4), (7): the tables are updated by 0.26% from 1.3.2017, by 0.25%
-- more from 1.3.2019 and 0.75% more from 1.10.2019, each over the tables of
-- the eve of the signing — 0.51% and 1.26% in all, added, not compounded.
-- The updated tables are annexes ב1–ב30, ג1–ג30 and ד1–ד30 (data at the
-- end, checked there against this rule).
@ref akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_1 akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_1/p2 akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_4 akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_4/p2 akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_7 akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_7/p2
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the total update of the tables under §7(ה) on` d IS
    sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `allocation rate`) (filter (GIVEN a YIELD d `is on or after` (a's `allocation from`)) `the September 2016 allocations`))

#ASSERT `the total update of the tables under §7(ה) on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019) EQUALS 0.51%
#ASSERT `the total update of the tables under §7(ה) on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2019) EQUALS 1.26%

GIVEN `a cell on the eve of the signing` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a reform table cell under §7(ה)` `a cell on the eve of the signing` d IS
    `a cell on the eve of the signing` `increased by` (`the total update of the tables under §7(ה) on` d)

#ASSERT `a reform table cell under §7(ה)` 10000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2019) EQUALS 10126

-- (ה)(2)(א), (5), (8): the 2016 percentage supplement ("תוספת אחוזית
-- 2016"), on the combined salary and the 2001, 2008 and 2011 supplements:
-- 0.26% from 1.3.2017, raised by addition to 0.51% from 1.3.2019 and to
-- 1.26% from 1.10.2019. (ב): the 2001 supplement is computed first (on a
-- base without the later ones), then the 2008, then the 2011, then this.
@ref akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_2__cls_a akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_2__cls_b akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_5 akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_8
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 percentage supplement rate on` d IS
    `the total update of the tables under §7(ה) on` d

GIVEN `the combined salary` IS A NUMBER
      `the 2001 supplement` IS A NUMBER @desc computed on a base without the 2008, 2011 or 2016 percentage supplements
      `the 2008 supplement` IS A NUMBER @desc computed on a base without the 2011 or 2016 percentage supplements
      `the 2011 supplement` IS A NUMBER @desc computed on a base without the 2016 percentage supplement
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 percentage supplement` `the combined salary` `the 2001 supplement` `the 2008 supplement` `the 2011 supplement` d IS
    `the 2016 percentage supplement rate on` d TIMES (`the combined salary` PLUS `the 2001 supplement` PLUS `the 2008 supplement` PLUS `the 2011 supplement`)

#ASSERT `the 2016 percentage supplement` 10000 0 0 0 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `the 2016 percentage supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2017) EQUALS 0

-- (ה)(2)(ג)–(ה): not in topping up to the minimum wage (an excluded
-- supplement); salary for every purpose, in the percentage supplements of
-- the combined salary save the 2001, 2008 and 2011, the hour value,
-- severance pay, accrual-pension and study-fund contributions; in the
-- determining salary (the government's statement).
@ref akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_2__cls_c akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_2__cls_d akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_2__cls_e
GIVEN p IS A `September 2016 salary purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2016 percentage supplement counts for` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `topping up to the minimum wage` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the base of every pay supplement, by percentage or in shekels` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the salary base of the combined-salary tables` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `provident-fund contributions of every kind` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the payment under §31(ד) of the base agreement` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- (ה)(2)(ו) with its definition: the shekel supplements off the reform are
-- updated by 0.26% from 1.3.2017 — every shekel supplement paid off the
-- reform on the eve of the signing, save those with another updating
-- mechanism and the minimum-wage top-up; this agreement's shekel supplement
-- has its own (¶3). The first part's record of a shekel supplement, imported.
@ref akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_2__cls_f akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_2/p3
GIVEN s IS A `shekel supplement`, `the amount on the eve` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a shekel supplement off the reform under §7(ה)` s `the amount on the eve` d IS
    IF `is one of the shekel supplements` s AND d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017)
    THEN `the amount on the eve` `increased by` (0.26%)
    ELSE `the amount on the eve`

`this agreement's shekel supplement is updated with the others` MEANS FALSE

-- (ה)(3), (6), (9): the payments are made from the salary for March 2019,
-- … and at the latest the next month's, with the differences: the March
-- 2017, March 2019 and October 2019 salaries, a month's grace each.
@ref akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_3 akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_6 akn:art_7__para_e__subpara_9
GIVEN a IS A `September 2016 allocation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the last salary month §7(ה) pays an allocation in` a IS
    `September 2016 salary month` (DATE_YEAR (a's `allocation from`)) (DATE_MONTH (a's `allocation from`)) PLUS 1

#ASSERT map `the last salary month §7(ה) pays an allocation in` `the September 2016 allocations` EQUALS LIST (`September 2016 salary month` 2017 4), (`September 2016 salary month` 2019 4), (`September 2016 salary month` 2019 11)

-- (ו): (ב)–(ד) take nothing from industrial peace (§12); no labour dispute
-- is declared and no organisational measures are taken for want of an
-- agreement on the allocation.
@ref akn:art_7__para_f
`no dispute over §7's allocation` MEANS
    PARTY `the teachers' union`
    SHANT `declare a labour dispute or take organisational measures over the allocation of §7(ב)–(ד)`

§§ `8 מענק חד פעמי`

-- (א): one employed as a teaching employee in the State's service
-- continuously from 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 ("התקופה הקובעת") is entitled, in
-- the salary for January 2017 and no later than February's, to a one-time
-- grant of 1,000 only. (ו)–(ח): maternity and parenthood (as §6 of the
-- Women's Employment Law means it; 26 weeks as a rule) does not break the
-- continuity, and the other conditions apply to those in it; (ט) so for a
-- man in it. (י): reserve duty; (יא): sick leave under the takanon's
-- §1.25.3; (יב): an approved paid absence — none breaks it. The circular
-- 2016-1-13 asked the same, in the same periods: its record of a teaching
-- employee is imported. Unlike the circular's §13, (יג) does not name sick
-- leave without pay, so it is sick leave and keeps the continuity (יא).
@ref akn:art_8__para_a akn:art_8__para_f akn:art_8__para_f/p2 akn:art_8__para_f/p3 akn:art_8__para_g akn:art_8__para_h akn:art_8__para_i akn:art_8__para_j akn:art_8__para_ja akn:art_8__para_jb
`the second one-time grant for a full position` MEANS 1000

GIVEN k IS AN `absence kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `keeps the continuity under §8` k IF
    NOT k EQUALS `unpaid leave or an absence treated as one`

-- (ו) ¶2: the birth and parenthood period under the Women's Work Law is
-- 26 weeks as a rule, unless §6 extends it.
@ref akn:art_8__para_f/p2
`the birth and parenthood period's length as §8(ו) prints it, in weeks` MEANS 26

-- The Women's Work Law (imported): the 26 weeks printed are §6(ב)(1)'s
-- period for one with twelve months with the employer (the "as a rule";
-- §6(ב)(5) gives 15 to one with fewer), and keeping the period in the
-- grant's count gives at least what §6(ט) keeps — that the period harms no
-- right that turns on seniority. The floor is met; §23 keeps the rest.
`§8's birth and parenthood period meets the Women's Work Law` MEANS
        `the birth and parenthood period's length as §8(ו) prints it, in weeks` EQUALS `weeks of the birth and parenthood period` 12
    AND `keeps the continuity under §8` `maternity leave`
    AND `the birth and parenthood period harms no right that turns on seniority`
#ASSERT `§8's birth and parenthood period meets the Women's Work Law`

GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `takes §8(יג)'s route` t IF
    elem `unpaid leave or an absence treated as one` (t's `absences in the qualifying period`)

GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualifies under §8(א)` t IF
        t's `a teaching employee in the state service`
    AND t's `employed throughout 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 but for absences`
    AND all `keeps the continuity under §8` (t's `absences in the qualifying period`)

-- (יג)(1): one on unpaid leave, or an absence treated as one, in the
-- period: entitled if, from 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016, salary was due for 4 full
-- months of work and at least one more day, in a row, full-time or not.
@ref akn:art_8__para_jc akn:art_8__para_jc__subpara_1
GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualifies under §8(יג)` t IF
        t's `a teaching employee in the state service`
    AND (   t's `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` AT LEAST 5
         OR (t's `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` AT LEAST 4 AND t's `and at least one salaried day more`))

GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualifies for the second one-time grant` t IF
    IF `takes §8(יג)'s route` t
    THEN `qualifies under §8(יג)` t
    ELSE `qualifies under §8(א)` t

-- (ב): the 1,000 is for a full position; each teacher's in proportion to
-- the representative monthly average of the position from 1.12.2014 to
-- 30.11.2015; ¶2: one employed part-time in only part of that period, but
-- continuously in the determining period, over the period employed. (יג)(2):
-- on (יג)'s route, the part of it employed; (3) if no salary at all was
-- due in it, 1.12.2015–30.11.2016.
-- F-ofek-hadash-september-2016-f: ¶2 speaks of a part-time teacher only, as
-- the circular's §2 did (F-2016-02-22_sachar_2016-1-13_maanak-hora-b); the
-- reading adopted is the circular's (convention reading.consistent): the
-- average over the months employed, for every teacher. No ceiling is set
-- (convention position.above-full).
@ref akn:art_8__para_b akn:art_8__para_b/p2 akn:art_8__para_jc__subpara_2 akn:art_8__para_jc__subpara_3
GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position the second grant is computed on` t IS
    IF `takes §8(יג)'s route` t AND NOT t's `any salary due from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`
    THEN t's `average position from 1.12.2015 to 30.11.2016`
    ELSE t's `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`

GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the second one-time grant` t IS
    IF `qualifies for the second one-time grant` t
    THEN `the second one-time grant for a full position` `pro rata to a position of` (`the position the second grant is computed on` t)
    ELSE 0

GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the second grant averaged over the twelve months` t IS
    `the second one-time grant for a full position`
        TIMES t's `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`
        TIMES t's `months employed from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`
        DIVIDED BY 12

`§8(ב) leaves a full-timer employed part of the period between two readings` MEANS
        `the second one-time grant` `a full-time teacher who joined on 1.9.2015` EQUALS 1000
    AND `the second grant averaged over the twelve months` `a full-time teacher who joined on 1.9.2015` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `§8(ב) leaves a full-timer employed part of the period between two readings`

-- With the circular's teachers: the same grant twice, the framework's 2,000.
#ASSERT `the second one-time grant` `a full-time teacher all year` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the second one-time grant` `a teacher at 75% on maternity leave` EQUALS 750
#ASSERT `the second one-time grant` `a teacher on unpaid leave after four months` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the second one-time grant` `a teacher on unpaid leave after four months and a day` EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `the one-time grant` `a full-time teacher all year` PLUS `the second one-time grant` `a full-time teacher all year` EQUALS `the framework's one-time grant`

-- (ג)–(ה): the grant is not salary for any purpose: not in the hour value,
-- substitution and school-activity hours, the reduction for an hour of
-- absence, the payment of §33(ד), severance pay, nor any provident-fund
-- contribution (study fund, pension fund, managers' insurance); not in
-- topping up to the minimum wage (ד); and it changes nothing in the salary
-- base of the combined-salary tables in force "on the eve of publishing
-- this circular" (ה) — the circular's words, kept in the agreement.
@ref akn:art_8__para_c akn:art_8__para_d akn:art_8__para_e
GIVEN p IS A `September 2016 salary purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the second one-time grant counts for` p IF
    FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the second one-time grant counts for` `severance pay under the Severance Pay Law`

-- (יג)(4) and (א): paid in the salary for January 2017, at the latest
-- February's. (יד): one who at the time of payment is on sick leave
-- without salary, in maternity and parenthood, on unpaid leave, or absent
-- for a work injury not charged to sick leave: in the first salary on the
-- return to work, at the latest the next. (טו): one whose employment ends
-- before: in the last salary.
-- not weighed against `the Sick Pay Law`: §8(יא) keeps sick leave from
-- breaking the second grant's run, and (יד)(1) puts off its payment to one
-- on sick leave without salary to his return; the law sets sick pay and the
-- days that accrue for it, and nothing on a grant, so neither rules on what
-- the law puts a floor under.

DECLARE `away at the time of the second grant` IS ONE OF
    `at work at the time of the grant`
    `on sick leave without salary at the time of the grant`
    `in maternity and parenthood at the time of the grant`
    `on unpaid leave at the time of the grant`
    `absent for a work injury not charged to sick leave at the time of the grant`
    `left before the time of the grant`

@ref akn:art_8__para_jc__subpara_4 akn:art_8__para_jd akn:art_8__para_jd__subpara_1 akn:art_8__para_jd__subpara_2 akn:art_8__para_jd__subpara_3 akn:art_8__para_jd__subpara_4 akn:art_8__para_if
GIVEN away IS AN `away at the time of the second grant`
      `the salary month of the return or the last salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the last salary month for the second grant` away `the salary month of the return or the last salary` IS
    CONSIDER away
    WHEN `at work at the time of the grant` THEN `September 2016 salary month` 2017 2
    WHEN `left before the time of the grant` THEN `the salary month of the return or the last salary`
    OTHERWISE `the salary month of the return or the last salary` PLUS 1

#ASSERT `the last salary month for the second grant` `at work at the time of the grant` 0 EQUALS `September 2016 salary month` 2017 2
#ASSERT `the last salary month for the second grant` `in maternity and parenthood at the time of the grant` (`September 2016 salary month` 2017 5) EQUALS `September 2016 salary month` 2017 6

@ref akn:art_8__para_a
`paying the second one-time grant` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `pay the second one-time grant`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the State` BECAUSE "§8: the grant is paid by the salary for February 2017, or as (יד)–(טו) set"

-- The determining period is itself four months and one day: (יג)(1)'s
-- threshold is its length.
#ASSERT DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2016) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2015) PLUS 1 EQUALS 123

§§ `9 תיקון הסכם 2016 והחלפת הוראות ההסכם מיום 31.8.2016`

-- ¶1–¶2: the cost of §5(א) of the 2016 agreement is allocated otherwise, as
-- this agreement shows; so, from 1.9.2016: (א) §7(א) and (ב) of the 2016
-- agreement are void, and so is §4 of the agreement of 31.8.2016, which
-- amended its §5(א); (ב) its §6 (the salary base) is relevant only for §7
-- here; (ג) its §§7 and 8 do not apply; (ד) its §9 is no longer relevant;
-- (ה) §4 here replaces §4 of the agreement of 31.8.2016.
DECLARE `clause of the 2016 agreement` IS ONE OF
    `its §5(א), the allocation`
    `its §6, the salary base`
    `its §7(א)–(ב), the tables and the 2016 protection supplement`
    `its §7(ג)–(ד), the protection supplement's reduction`
    `its §8, the one-time promotion`
    `its §9, the general provisions`
    `another of its clauses`

@ref akn:art_9/p1 akn:art_9/p2 akn:art_9__para_a akn:art_9__para_b akn:art_9__para_c akn:art_9__para_d akn:art_9__para_e
GIVEN c IS A `clause of the 2016 agreement`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a clause of the 2016 agreement governs under §9` c d IF
    IF d `is on or after` `the September 2016 promotion rules start`
    THEN CONSIDER c
         WHEN `another of its clauses` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE
    ELSE TRUE

-- (ב): the 2016 agreement's salary base still serves §7 here.
`the 2016 salary base still serves §7 of the September 2016 agreement` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_9__para_a akn:art_9__para_e
`the agreement of 31.8.2016's §4 governs from 1.9.2016` MEANS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `a clause of the 2016 agreement governs under §9` `its §8, the one-time promotion` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016)
#ASSERT `a clause of the 2016 agreement governs under §9` `its §8, the one-time promotion` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2016)
#ASSERT `a clause of the 2016 agreement governs under §9` `another of its clauses` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016)

§§ `10 גמלאים בפנסיה תקציבית`

-- (א): the Treasury announces it intends to circulate an amendment of the
-- State Service (Pensions) Law, on these principles: (1) for one who
-- retired between 1.1.2013 and 30.9.2019 graded on the teaching employees'
-- scale ("פורש זכאי"); (2) the determining salary grows by Y = X·A + X·B·C:
-- X the coefficient for the month of retirement by annex ה' (data at the
-- end, `X, the coefficient of annex ה' on`; the agreement of 19.3.2017
-- replaces it with its own annex א'); A
-- the full shekel supplement for the retiree's grade; B the full rate of
-- the percentage supplement or the table update; C the determining salary
-- without the supplements of (א)–(ד); (3) for one moved from the old terms
-- to the reform, C is the pension agreement's; (4) each supplement by
-- itself, Y the sum; (5) an increase of an existing supplement counts by
-- the increase; (6) gradually, by annex ה'.
@ref akn:art_10__para_a akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_1
GIVEN `retired on` IS A DATE, `graded on the teaching employees' scale on the eve` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an eligible retiree under §10 of the September 2016 agreement` `retired on` `graded on the teaching employees' scale on the eve` IF
        `retired on` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013)
    AND `retired on` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2019)
    AND `graded on the teaching employees' scale on the eve`

@desc One supplement as §10(א)(2)–(5) count it for a retiree.
DECLARE `supplement for the retiree's increase` HAS
    `A, the full shekel amount`   IS A NUMBER @desc 0 for a percentage supplement
    `B, the full rate`            IS A NUMBER @desc 0 for a shekel supplement; a table update counts as one

@ref akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_2/p3 akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_2/p4 akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_2/p5 akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_2/p6 akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_2__cls_a akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_2__cls_b akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_2__cls_c akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_2__cls_d akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_3 akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_4 akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_5 akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_5/p2 akn:art_10__para_a__subpara_6
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER @desc the determining salary without convalescence and clothing pay, supplements with another updating mechanism, the minimum-wage top-up and supplements first paid after 31.12.2015 (for one moved to the reform, the pension agreement's determining salary)
      supplements IS A LIST OF `supplement for the retiree's increase`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Y, the increase of the determining salary under §10 of the September 2016 agreement` x c supplements IS
    sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD (x TIMES s's `A, the full shekel amount`) PLUS (x TIMES s's `B, the full rate` TIMES c)) supplements)

#ASSERT `Y, the increase of the determining salary under §10 of the September 2016 agreement` 0.5 10000 (LIST `supplement for the retiree's increase` 100 0, `supplement for the retiree's increase` 0 (0.26%)) EQUALS 63

-- (ב): the union accepts the principles and supports the legislation as
-- needed (1); once it is passed, no demand to increase the determining
-- salary, or for a supplement or benefit, for these costs or for the
-- period to 30.6.2018 (2).
@ref akn:art_10__para_b akn:art_10__para_b__subpara_1
`the union supports the pensions amendment` MEANS
    PARTY `the teachers' union`
    MUST  `support the legislation of §10(א)`

@ref akn:art_10__para_b__subpara_2
GIVEN `the amendment is passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `September 2016 action`
DECIDE `no further pension demand` `the amendment is passed` IS
    IF `the amendment is passed`
    THEN PARTY `the teachers' union`
         SHANT `demand a further increase of the determining salary, a supplement or a benefit for these costs`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (ג): for an eligible retiree entitled to the jubilee grant (of the
-- agreement of 19.9.1994 as amended on 27.8.2008), the salary its
-- component is computed on grows by Y, gradually as the determining salary
-- does, if the supplements making Y count for the hour value; its day of
-- payment is unchanged.
@ref akn:art_10__para_c akn:art_10__para_c/p2 akn:art_10__para_c/p3
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, `Y's supplements count for the hour value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the jubilee grant base's increase` y `Y's supplements count for the hour value` IS
    IF `Y's supplements count for the hour value` THEN y ELSE 0

-- (ד)–(ה): (א)–(ג) apply only once the allocation of §7(ב)–(ד) is agreed,
-- and only if every shekel supplement (A) and percentage supplement (B)
-- paid to a reform teacher is what he would be paid off the reform (a
-- table update counting as a percentage supplement); otherwise the parties
-- discuss the pensioners' arrangement, at no further cost. (ו): nothing in
-- (ה) takes from exhaustion (§11) or industrial peace (§12).
@ref akn:art_10__para_d akn:art_10__para_d__subpara_1 akn:art_10__para_d__subpara_2 akn:art_10__para_e
GIVEN `§7's allocation is agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A is the same on and off the reform` IS A BOOLEAN
      `B is the same on and off the reform` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§10(א)–(ג) of the September 2016 agreement apply` `§7's allocation is agreed` `A is the same on and off the reform` `B is the same on and off the reform` IF
    `§7's allocation is agreed` AND `A is the same on and off the reform` AND `B is the same on and off the reform`

@ref akn:art_10__para_e/p2 akn:art_10__para_f
`discussing the pensioners otherwise` MEANS
    (PARTY `the State`
     MAY   `discuss the pensioners' arrangement without further cost`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     MAY   `discuss the pensioners' arrangement without further cost`)

#ASSERT NOT `§10(א)–(ג) of the September 2016 agreement apply` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§§ `11 מיצוי תביעות`

-- (א): the agreement fully exhausts the parties' claims to 30.6.2018; among
-- them every claim under §17(ג) of the 2013 agreement and §155(א) of the
-- base agreement (imported: the framework's cost is no longer open), the
-- framework agreements of 12.1.2011, 18.4.2016 and 8.8.2016, and §9(א) of
-- the 2016 agreement; no further negotiation on economic demands for the
-- period, §15 of the 2013 agreement included.
@ref akn:art_11__para_a akn:art_11__para_a/p2 akn:art_11__para_a/p3 akn:art_11__para_a/p4
`the September 2016 agreement exhausts the claims to` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2018

GIVEN m IS A `matter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may still be negotiated after the September 2016 agreement` m IF
    `may be negotiated` m AND NOT m EQUALS `the cost of a framework agreement`

#ASSERT `may be negotiated` `the cost of a framework agreement`
#ASSERT NOT `may still be negotiated after the September 2016 agreement` `the cost of a framework agreement`

-- (ב)–(ג): save the negotiation for the populations of §155(ב) for whom no
-- agreement exhausting it was yet signed — (1) teaching employees in
-- guidance roles, (2) principals of institutions for gifted pupils — and
-- the negotiation under §10 of the colleges' agreement of 7.5.2015 (whose
-- §§13–14 stand). (ד): no other exhaustion or industrial peace is touched.
DECLARE `matter left open by §11 of the September 2016 agreement` IS ONE OF
    `the reform for teaching employees in guidance roles`
    `the reform for principals of institutions for gifted pupils`
    `the negotiation under §10 of the colleges' agreement of 7.5.2015`
    `another economic demand for the period`

@ref akn:art_11__para_b akn:art_11__para_b/p2 akn:art_11__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_11__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_11__para_c akn:art_11__para_d
GIVEN m IS A `matter left open by §11 of the September 2016 agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§11 of the September 2016 agreement leaves open` m IF
    NOT m EQUALS `another economic demand for the period`

@ref akn:art_11__para_a/p4
`no further economic demands to 30.6.2018` MEANS
    (PARTY `the State`
     SHANT `negotiate further economic demands for the period to 30.6.2018`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `negotiate further economic demands for the period to 30.6.2018`)

§§ `12 שקט תעשייתי`

-- (א): in the agreement's period neither party strikes, locks out or
-- disrupts work over what it settles; (ב) not over §11(ב)–(ג); (ג): the
-- union's notice of a labour dispute of 6.12.2015 is void.
@ref akn:art_12__para_a akn:art_12__para_b
`industrial peace under the September 2016 agreement` MEANS
    (PARTY `the State`
     SHANT `strike, lock out or disrupt work over a matter the September 2016 agreement settles`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `strike, lock out or disrupt work over a matter the September 2016 agreement settles`)

GIVEN m IS A `matter left open by §11 of the September 2016 agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§12's industrial peace covers` m IF
    NOT `§11 of the September 2016 agreement leaves open` m

@ref akn:art_12__para_c
GIVEN `declared on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a union dispute notice stands under the September 2016 agreement` `declared on` IF
    `a union dispute notice stands under the 2016 agreement` `declared on`

#ASSERT NOT `a union dispute notice stands under the September 2016 agreement` (DATE_FROM_DMY 6 12 2015)

§§ `13–16 כללי, הסכמים קודמים, יישוב חילוקי דעות, רישום`

-- §13: nothing takes from the wages commissioner's letter to the union's
-- secretary-general of 10.9.2007 on the reform, without prejudice to either
-- party's claims on it.
@ref akn:art_13/p1
`the September 2016 agreement takes from the letter of 10.9.2007` MEANS FALSE

-- §14: the terms of earlier agreements, arrangements and written
-- undertakings stand in the agreement's period, unless expressly or
-- impliedly amended or cancelled by it.
@ref akn:art_14/p1
GIVEN `amended or cancelled by this agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an earlier term stands under the September 2016 agreement` `amended or cancelled by this agreement` IF
    NOT `amended or cancelled by this agreement`

-- §15: the follow-up committee of the wages commissioner, the
-- director-general and the union's secretary-general decides disputes on
-- the agreement, finally and bindingly.
@ref akn:art_15/p1
`the September 2016 agreement's follow-up committee` MEANS LIST `the wages commissioner`, `the director-general`, `the union's secretary-general`

GIVEN `the committee's decision` IS A STRING, `a party's reading` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `what binds the parties of the September 2016 agreement` `the committee's decision` `a party's reading` IS
    `the committee's decision`

-- §16: submitted for registration as a special collective agreement (no
-- deadline: convention dates.no-deadline).
@ref akn:art_16/p1
`registering the September 2016 agreement` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `submit the agreement for registration as a special collective agreement`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:conclusions/p1 The State's signature heading; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p2 The union's signature heading; no rule.

§§ `נספחים א'–ד' — טבלאות השכר`

-- The tables the agreement attaches (pp. 17–59 of the copy): annexes
-- א'1–א'7, §5(א)'s tables from 1.9.2016 — the BA and MA salary tables
-- (codes 101, 102) and the conversion tables of the existing teachers (BA,
-- MA, בכיר, מוסמך, בלתי מוסמך: codes 101, 102, 104, 105, 106); and annexes
-- ב'1–ב'30, ג'1–ג'30 and ד'1–ד'30, §7(ה)'s tables as updated from 1.3.2017,
-- 1.3.2019 and 1.10.2019 — the same seven teachers' tables, the new and
-- existing principals', junior-high principals' and deputies' tables
-- (8–22) and the supervisors' and headquarters staff's (23–30). Each is
-- DATA, cell for cell as the corpus publishes it, written by its grades and
-- each row's amounts (`a published grid`, tables-common.l4, generated by
-- tools/table_l4.py; tests/test_tables.py holds every cell by position).
-- A principal's rank is its number (א 1 … ד 4, א+ 1.5 …); a supervisor's
-- table prints one row and no label (row 0). Every table prints its
-- amounts in whole shekels but annex א'6, which prints agorot.
--
-- Annexes ב–ד never governed: the agreement of 19.3.2017 (§2(ז), in its
-- own file) voids §7, the section that attaches them, and allocates its
-- cost otherwise. They are held as the text this agreement printed; the
-- checks below say only that they are what §7(ה) as signed makes, and no
-- lookup of the tables in force reads them (tables-in-force-common.l4).
--
-- What the corpus marks and this reading takes as given: ב'1 and ב'2 print
-- "טבלה מעודכנת החל מיום 1.3.2019" [כך במקור], where §7(ה)(1) attaches the
-- ב tables from 1.3.2017 and their cells are the 0.26% update (checked
-- below) — they are read as from 1.3.2017; ב'7 prints "#REF!" [כך במקור]
-- for the step over grades 2–5, which is no step; ד'15–ד'18 carry the
-- titles of ד'11–ד'14 [כך במקור] over the junior-high principals' cells.
-- The cells the corpus marks illegible ([לא קריא]) are not in their rows
-- (`why the annexes' illegible cells of 30.9.2016 are not here`).

