-- The windows' first days, as the header prints them.
`the windows of annex ה' begin on` MEANS
    LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2018, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2019

-- X of a retiree on a day: the row of his last active month, the column of
-- the window the day is in; before the first window, none.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `X, the coefficient of annex ה' on` y m d IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the last active year of annex ה'` EQUALS y AND r's `the last active month of annex ה'` EQUALS m) `annex ה' of 30.9.2016`
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER drop (count (filter (GIVEN w YIELD d `is on or after` w) `the windows of annex ה' begin on`) MINUS 1) (r's `X in each window of annex ה'`)
        WHEN x FOLLOWED BY more THEN
            IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) THEN x ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING

#ASSERT `X, the coefficient of annex ה' on` 2013 1 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) EQUALS JUST (1.52%)
#ASSERT `X, the coefficient of annex ה' on` 2016 9 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `X, the coefficient of annex ה' on` 2013 1 (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2016) EQUALS NOTHING

-- What the annex says of itself. (1) Every month from 1.2013 to 9.2019,
-- once and in order, six windows each.
#ASSERT count `annex ה' of 30.9.2016` EQUALS 81
#ASSERT map (GIVEN r YIELD `September 2016 salary month` (r's `the last active year of annex ה'`) (r's `the last active month of annex ה'`)) `annex ה' of 30.9.2016` EQUALS map (GIVEN i YIELD `September 2016 salary month` 2013 1 PLUS i) (range 0 80)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD count (r's `X in each window of annex ה'`) EQUALS 6) `annex ה' of 30.9.2016`

-- (2) A row is blank exactly under the windows that began by the first of
-- its month, and prints X under every other.
GIVEN r IS AN `annex ה' row of 30.9.2016`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is blank exactly under the windows begun by its month` r IS
    and (zipWith (GIVEN w, x YIELD (x EQUALS NOTHING) EQUALS ((DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (r's `the last active month of annex ה'`) (r's `the last active year of annex ה'`)) `is on or after` w))
                 `the windows of annex ה' begin on` (r's `X in each window of annex ה'`))

#ASSERT all `is blank exactly under the windows begun by its month` `annex ה' of 30.9.2016`

-- (3) No rule states it, but the table shows its making: the n-th month's
-- X in the last window, which no earlier window caps, is n/66 to the
-- hundredth of a point for every month before the first window (the
-- first 44 rows).
#ASSERT all (GIVEN i YIELD
                 CONSIDER drop i `annex ה' of 30.9.2016`
                 WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
                     CONSIDER drop 5 (r's `X in each window of annex ה'`)
                     WHEN x FOLLOWED BY none THEN x EQUALS JUST (`to the nearest` ((i PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 66) 0.0001)
                     WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
                 WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE)
            (range 0 43)

§§ `בדיקת הנספחים`

-- (1) The days the tables print: א' §5(א)'s determining date; ב, ג and ד
-- the days of §7(ה)(1), (4) and (7) — save ב'1 and ב'2, which print
-- 1.3.2019 [כך במקור] and are read as from 1.3.2017.
GIVEN ts IS A LIST OF `published table`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
DECIDE `the days printed under` ts IS
    nub (map (GIVEN t YIELD t's `published table from`) ts)

#ASSERT `the days printed under` `annexes א' of 30.9.2016` EQUALS LIST `the September 2016 determining date`
#ASSERT `the days printed under` (drop 2 `annexes ב' of 30.9.2016`) EQUALS LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017
#ASSERT `the days printed under` (take 2 `annexes ב' of 30.9.2016`) EQUALS LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019
#ASSERT `the days printed under` `annexes ג' of 30.9.2016` EQUALS LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019
#ASSERT `the days printed under` `annexes ד' of 30.9.2016` EQUALS LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2019
#ASSERT map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `allocation from`) `the September 2016 allocations` EQUALS LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019, DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2019
#ASSERT map count (LIST `annexes ב' of 30.9.2016`, `annexes ג' of 30.9.2016`, `annexes ד' of 30.9.2016`) EQUALS LIST 30, 30, 30

-- (2) §7(ה)(1), (4), (7): each updated teachers' table is its 1.9.2016 table
-- raised by 0.26%, 0.51% and 1.26%, over the tables of the eve of the
-- signing. Annexes א' print whole shekels (א'6 agorot), so a cell raised
-- from one to the shekel is at most a shekel off the printed cell.
GIVEN other IS A `published table`, factor IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER AND NUMBER TO MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the annex cell of` other `raised by` factor `to the shekel` IS
    GIVEN l, g YIELD
        CONSIDER `the published cell at` other l g
        WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (`to the nearest whole` (x TIMES factor))
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the factor §7(ה) raises the tables of the eve by on` d IS
    1 PLUS `the total update of the tables under §7(ה) on` d

GIVEN updated IS A LIST OF `published table`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `published cell check`
DECIDE `the teachers' tables of` updated `beside annexes א' raised on` d IS
    concat (zipWith (GIVEN u, a YIELD `the published cells beside` (`the annex cell of` a `raised by` (`the factor §7(ה) raises the tables of the eve by on` d) `to the shekel`) `in` u)
                    (take 7 updated) `annexes א' of 30.9.2016`)

`the ב tables beside annexes א'` MEANS `the teachers' tables of` `annexes ב' of 30.9.2016` `beside annexes א' raised on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017)
`the ג tables beside annexes א'` MEANS `the teachers' tables of` `annexes ג' of 30.9.2016` `beside annexes א' raised on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019)
`the ד tables beside annexes א'` MEANS `the teachers' tables of` `annexes ד' of 30.9.2016` `beside annexes א' raised on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2019)

-- Every cell a 1.9.2016 cell reaches is checked (3,506, 3,506 and 3,505:
-- the illegible ones are not); 720, 702 and 726 miss, each by a shekel.
#ASSERT map count (LIST `the ב tables beside annexes א'`, `the ג tables beside annexes א'`, `the ד tables beside annexes א'`) EQUALS LIST 3506, 3506, 3505
#ASSERT map (GIVEN cs YIELD count (`the published misses in` cs)) (LIST `the ב tables beside annexes א'`, `the ג tables beside annexes א'`, `the ד tables beside annexes א'`) EQUALS LIST 720, 702, 726
#ASSERT map `the published worst miss in` (LIST `the ב tables beside annexes א'`, `the ג tables beside annexes א'`, `the ד tables beside annexes א'`) EQUALS LIST 100, 100, 100

-- (3) The principals', deputies' and supervisors' tables (8–30) have no
-- 1.9.2016 twin among the annexes: ג and ד are each ב raised by what §7(ה)
-- adds after 1.3.2017 (1.0051/1.0026 and 1.0126/1.0026), and each printed
-- cell is a shekel at most off the ב cell so raised.
GIVEN later IS A LIST OF `published table`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `published cell check`
DECIDE `the managers' tables of` later `beside annexes ב' raised to` d IS
    concat (zipWith (GIVEN u, b YIELD `the published cells beside` (`the annex cell of` b `raised by` (`the factor §7(ה) raises the tables of the eve by on` d DIVIDED BY `the factor §7(ה) raises the tables of the eve by on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017)) `to the shekel`) `in` u)
                    (drop 7 later) (drop 7 `annexes ב' of 30.9.2016`))

`the managers' ג tables beside ב` MEANS `the managers' tables of` `annexes ג' of 30.9.2016` `beside annexes ב' raised to` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019)
`the managers' ד tables beside ב` MEANS `the managers' tables of` `annexes ד' of 30.9.2016` `beside annexes ב' raised to` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2019)

#ASSERT map count (LIST `the managers' ג tables beside ב`, `the managers' ד tables beside ב`) EQUALS LIST 780, 780
#ASSERT map (GIVEN cs YIELD count (`the published misses in` cs)) (LIST `the managers' ג tables beside ב`, `the managers' ד tables beside ב`) EQUALS LIST 187, 212
#ASSERT map `the published worst miss in` (LIST `the managers' ג tables beside ב`, `the managers' ד tables beside ב`) EQUALS LIST 100, 100

-- (4) Annex א'7 (בלתי מוסמך, code 106) steps grade 7 by 7.8% and grades 8
-- and 9 by 8.5%, as the 2016 agreement's annexes of 22.2.2016 (imported)
-- step every table; annexes א'1–א'6 step every grade by 7.5%. א'7 is the
-- 2016 agreement's annex א'7 to the shekel, cell for cell (save the
-- cells printed at an exact half, which it takes down).
#ASSERT map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `published rate`) ((`annex א'7 of 30.9.2016`)'s `published grade rates`) EQUALS LIST (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.8%), (8.5%), (8.5%)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD all (GIVEN s YIELD s's `published rate` EQUALS 7.5%) (t's `published grade rates`)) (take 6 `annexes א' of 30.9.2016`)

GIVEN l IS A NUMBER, g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 agreement's annex א'7 cell to the shekel` l g IS
    CONSIDER `the pay at grade` g (`the row labelled` `2016 annex א'7` l)
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (`to the nearest whole` x)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

`annex א'7 of 30.9.2016 beside the 2016 agreement's` MEANS
    `the published cells beside` `the 2016 agreement's annex א'7 cell to the shekel` `in` `annex א'7 of 30.9.2016`

GIVEN c IS A `published cell check`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2016 agreement prints a half shekel where annex א'7 of 30.9.2016 takes it down` c IF
        c's `agorot over the rule` EQUALS (0 MINUS 100)
    AND CONSIDER `the pay at grade` (c's `checked grade`) (`the row labelled` `2016 annex א'7` (c's `checked label`))
        WHEN JUST x THEN x MINUS FLOOR x EQUALS 0.5
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

#ASSERT count `annex א'7 of 30.9.2016 beside the 2016 agreement's` EQUALS `the published cell count of` `annex א'7 of 30.9.2016`
#ASSERT map (GIVEN c YIELD LIST (c's `checked label`), (c's `checked grade`)) (`the published misses in` `annex א'7 of 30.9.2016 beside the 2016 agreement's`) EQUALS LIST (LIST 10, 1), (LIST 10, 2.5), (LIST 22, 4), (LIST 33, 9)
#ASSERT all `the 2016 agreement prints a half shekel where annex א'7 of 30.9.2016 takes it down` (`the published misses in` `annex א'7 of 30.9.2016 beside the 2016 agreement's`)

-- The tables at work: §5(א)'s cell, and an existing teacher's placement on
-- a row of annex א'3.
#ASSERT `the cell of the September 2016 annexes א'1–א'7` 1 1 1 EQUALS JUST 5806
#ASSERT `the cell of the September 2016 annexes א'1–א'7` 8 1 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the September 2016 table salary on` 1 1 1 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) EMPTY EQUALS JUST 5806
#ASSERT `the September 2016 table salary on` 1 1 1 (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2016) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
